der that life is finite.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7140-a0fe-cbee188eaae0","description":"Hodie mihi, cras tibi","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-77af-9308-e79eba8a1bc0","description":"Cras es, noster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7e80-a6c2-343adb953348","description":"Tendit in, ardua virtus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7f0f-865c-dd4f0ebd6adf","description":"Vincit, qui patitur","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-73e6-b198-6920f3556f50","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Man is condemned to be free\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jean-Paul Sartre argued that people have no fixed essence and must take responsibility for the choices they make.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7327-9e88-14c86feb2d3b","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7569-91e2-2731f5c80eb8","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7292-8f0e-0180bd0da53b","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7973-b6dc-c4b05adf5bf3","description":"G. W. F. Hegel","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7f16-9efe-879fca8eff2e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What was the Starbucks chain of coffee shops named after?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Starbucks takes its name from Starbuck, the Pequod\u2019s first mate. The founders chose the name to evoke the seafaring history of coffee.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-75d0-8ef6-9478be7dcfcf","description":"A character in \'Moby Dick\'","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7e95-98d1-26947c17d852","description":"The owner\'s dog","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-710a-a944-bfc8865892c7","description":"A comic book hero","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7748-98b5-8d6ec0028e0d","description":"The owner\'s childhood friend","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-773b-982c-a729934e2088","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"According to the bible, who were the baby Jesus\'s first visitors?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Luke says the Shepherds went to Bethlehem after an angel announced Jesus\'s birth to them while they watched their flocks.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7abe-a224-24b6f499f0ba","description":"The Shepherds","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7667-abfd-50edfa191b4d","description":"Three Wise Men","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7bf4-930c-4c3b2d69f5ac","description":"King Herod","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-782b-ba78-a85bfb4ce288","description":"The Stable Boy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7050-a949-51c3bafbcc64","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In western societies, what is the traditional gift for a 10th wedding anniversary?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Tin\'s chemical symbol, Sn, comes from its Latin name, stannum.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-758b-a1ce-9229ab589c94","description":"Tin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7c95-9fa0-c7e13d3c0f7c","description":"Gold","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7d51-8ba1-4d0cf63bc7ae","description":"Silver","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-79b4-af97-8b5a556db3b2","description":"Bronze","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7c86-ac00-21039e35d1b8","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes Gregory Pincus?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Gregory Pincus worked with researcher Min Chueh Chang, and gynecologist John Rock led early clinical trials. Enovid became the first oral contraceptive approved in the United States.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7a02-a84c-467f16ba4841","description":"Biologist who created the oral contraceptive pill.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7b27-ae60-07aee341adc2","description":"Chemist and biologist who had a leading impact on the chemical revolution.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7154-936e-15929e1d453d","description":"A religious prophet.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7638-b888-0f348998da8e","description":"An influential figure in Sunni Islam.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7c5d-8cf4-95929f254d4e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Moroccan Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Moroccan Arabic is a variety of Arabic, which is classified in the Semitic branch of Afroasiatic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7ffc-8c2b-b3b0483356d5","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-71c3-801f-d976014de8ae","description":"Sino-Tibetan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-727c-a7cc-f4086327076e","description":"Niger\u2013Congo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-736b-888e-850690b15d55","description":"Austroasiatic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7a74-b7e9-00a3210b9f63","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who is referred to in the New Testament as \'the disciple Jesus loved\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John is traditionally identified as the beloved disciple, though the Gospel itself never gives that disciple\'s name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7cf4-a84c-54a2471d1164","description":"John","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7dd4-a9da-9d3aa832e621","description":"Matthew","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7585-bd13-bf21c1ff281c","description":"Mark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7f97-916d-2965ab6d9441","description":"Luke","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-799a-a73b-377806bc2690","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"On which Glouces