 in Greek mythology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7cbc-b2bc-ba38b2e8d6b8","description":"Leto","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7abd-8de6-891a2cded2e7","description":"Diana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-79e3-a230-4fddfb67edde","description":"Helen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-765b-9116-043ca60f1af5","description":"Aphrodite","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7d36-8a09-86ba5e97b652","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Pig Latin word is used to reject or cancel a statement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ixnay comes from \u201cnix,\u201d an informal word meaning to reject or prohibit; Pig Latin moves the opening consonant sound to the end and adds \u201cay.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7bd8-8e5b-f99ab070f79f","description":"Ixnay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-72cf-a05f-cb397f70bd9f","description":"Epay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-74eb-8fbb-6e2130c53a5a","description":"Ocklay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-770c-b8ea-22841f4cb31d","description":"Oopstay","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-75d9-b0d4-0794ae023c90","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Greek god invented the shepherd\'s flute and had a musical contest with Apollo?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Pan\u2019s reed pipes are commonly called panpipes. In the musical contest, Apollo played the lyre.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7df3-915c-87017cb79866","description":"Pan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7e00-8f57-91e00004179e","description":"Zeus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7247-99e9-f2099f8a8bdd","description":"Artemis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-77e5-abef-3e37843e67fb","description":"Athena","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556b-7439-9c56-3e2334c6c859","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c846499