eb-556c-7034-a8df-ef699651e3c6","description":"Honey, I\'m home","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72e4-a68b-eeac3684ea62","description":"Humiliation breeds subservience","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7fa0-af7c-143bb55f3461","description":"Humble is the child","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e55-afee-68eae09989fc","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the meaning of the Latin phrase \'Dum vita est, spes est\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Dum vita est, spes est\' is a Latin proverb meaning while there is life there is hope.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7aa9-90ea-cd7a9b0f3694","description":"While there is life there is hope","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-771f-8b0e-952ebe70d1d2","description":"Wisdom is power","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-78d9-9f2b-574c913c2a23","description":"Every man is the maker of his own fortune","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e78-82ec-91c1326fd2ee","description":"So it begins","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-770b-9935-bdc2a8f8bcdb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Entities should not be multiplied unnecessarily\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William of Ockham is associated with the principle commonly called Occam\u2019s razor, a rule of thumb for avoiding unnecessary assumptions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-76a5-9d45-84484e31d282","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77ab-88e6-ae1cdb9becbd","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79de-8da0-2d772f2ab456","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-70cf-a551-343325bebe61","description":"Spinoza","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72df-8a93-aa618ef6f680","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Even while they teach, men learn\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Seneca the Younger was a Roman statesman as well as a philosopher; his moral essays and letters remain among his best-known works.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79a5-974f-9b15da58adcc","description":"Seneca the Younger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7de9-bf95-4d1f3fba895f","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-713e-9b7a-64da922f662c","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77e4-a1d1-956eb9c23adc","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-728e-8eaa-e3b35c5b6762","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who was the ancient Egyptian goddess of the sky and queen of heaven ?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hathor was worshipped as a sky goddess and known as the Lady of Heaven. She was also associated with love, music, and motherhood.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7f55-8b13-305cc1f6deb0","description":"Hathor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-735d-9abf-b93302c69766","description":"Isis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-75b2-a352-6c9b1fbccc04","description":"Set","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7333-8c07-4553d86922dd","description":"Horus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-78b1-bc0b-d0d8c8a84e3a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is a wide cuff that is folded back and fastened with a cuff link called?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"French cuffs are traditionally considered more formal than button-fastened cuffs and use separate cuff links rather than sewn-on buttons.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7647-9260-8f84908d31dc","description":"A French cuff","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77aa-ab57-bca2e55bc352","description":"A button cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7dad-997d-c775395e3c64","description":"A barrel cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7617-94ba-5edc52e843b7","description":"A saville cuff","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-70cd-b43b-3b990488aa60","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'What is rational is actual and what is actual is rational\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The line appears in the preface to Hegel\u2019s Philosophy of Right, where he explored the relationship between reason and the world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7531-98c8-41f706b6bebd","description":"G. W. F. Hegel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ad9-8376-35d84cdb5f1a","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a0e-a5e9-9ad2659abdb6","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-776e-af9e-893228899544","description":"Democritus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-772e-a022-7651b35115ac","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 1982, which member of the British royal family gave birth to Prince William?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Princess Diana and Charles also had a younger son, Prince Harry, born in 1984.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a33-a024-df886a32a525","description":"Princess Diana","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-783d-a13b-a69a3dcd88e9","description":"Queen Elizabeth II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-734a-a71c-fee1f4810896","description":"Camilla Parker Bowles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ed3-acfc-51dd999075b5","description":"Sarah Ferguson","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-71b9-95c9-005e82896bea","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Berber is a language spoken in which of these countries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Berber languages are also known as Amazigh, and Morocco recognizes Tamazight as an official language.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a25-b770-7faa0979de7d","description":"Morocco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7935-8a8b-41c46aa9d4d0","description":"Kenya","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7af7-941b-db13e1e6fd12","description":"Tanzania","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-798d-8fca-46755d810fbd","description":"Sri Lanka","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e1b-8cce-4194daa1f3aa","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Whereof one cannot speak, thereof one must be silent\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ludwig Wittgenstein\u2019s Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus explores the limits of language and thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7eea-9129-eed1e59fe680","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7da6-a127-2d4f5fb97024","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7414-9d76-966842972c29","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-78b3-92b6-3290a660a5f2","description":"Immanuel Kant","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c13-8444-cd9e5f885582","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Overcome evil with good\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bono malum superate uses a plural command form, addressing more than one person, and echoes the injunction in Romans 12:21.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-74a3-ad91-591dcdfaa2cc","description":"Bono malum superate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-76cc-9a73-7527796093fb","description":"Bona fide","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-787e-a69c-1b3edd89a5a1","description":"Humilitas occidit superbiam","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7326-90b1-75151af0d290","description":"Fortiter et fideliter","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e7e-af5d-bab376f1bc31","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'There is only one thing a philosopher can be relied upon to do, and that is to contradict other philosophers\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William James was also a pioneering psychologist. His work helped shape pragmatism, which evaluates ideas partly by their practical consequences.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7032-86fb-eb04e74dc6c9","description":"William James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-771e-95ea-ef593f2c3a09","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7cd2-b02e-98c06166087a","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e3b-9769-b94377a6383e","description":"Martin Heidegger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-75bf-9445-9b003be35cea","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the shortest verse in the Bible?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jesus wept is John 11:35, which describes Jesus mourning at Lazarus\u2019s tomb. It is commonly cited as the shortest verse in English-language Bibles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7b05-81c2-6885af38eaa1","description":"Jesus wept","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72a2-a83e-ca4147244dca","description":"God spoke","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-779d-9d25-288d90e355a8","description":"No more","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e1c-9ee4-e90c84d64384","description":"Hallelujah","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-75a9-bc05-a6e579940eb3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 2002, which US city saw a number of coordinated sniper killings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 2002 Beltway sniper attacks took place across the Washington metropolitan area, including suburbs in Maryland and Virginia.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-75c7-818e-84e33e1b9135","description":"Washington, D.C.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a9d-9ef3-3350f8440839","description":"New York City","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7f53-b766-cae4e87be4c7","description":"Los Angeles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7dab-a659-a045296321e3","description":"Chicago","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7d2c-b891-71af0a13ccf7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Pax vobiscum\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\u201cPeace be with you\u201d is a traditional Christian liturgical greeting, often used during worship.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77fe-be17-3a3fe6209327","description":"Peace be with you","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7b0b-9f43-67c9aefbc802","description":"In good faith","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-787f-b741-53cd0d64e1dc","description":"And you, Brutus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-779f-880a-83b1849b79ed","description":"Nothing is arduous for the willing","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79a2-b35d-720b0339eca4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Tempora mutantur et nos mutamur in illis\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Tempora mutantur, et nos mutamur in illis\' means times change and we change with them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7741-9b16-757d5410db31","description":"The times are changing, and we change with them","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-73eb-9d29-05dc80ffdf8e","description":"What is said is done","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ef0-b423-1c618acab617","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ae0-acca-a00791620b3a","description":"Fortune favors the bold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-78e3-9a17-bb95ae19ed2e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the national animal of Scotland?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The unicorn appears as a supporter on Scotland\u2019s royal coat of arms, often shown chained because it was regarded as wild and untamable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ef7-a7e1-c09b022a79c5","description":"Unicorn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7dc2-85ec-c7d278cf0e48","description":"Lion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a14-9122-9857757a529d","description":"Dragon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77b6-ba7c-e270efeba3ae","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7591-87f7-9bb0952a1dd4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What charity organization works to protect the rights of indigenous and tribal peoples?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Survival International campaigns against the forced displacement of Indigenous peoples and defends their rights to their lands and ways of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-709b-9e79-dfcfed865d23","description":"Survival International","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7f87-8b3d-e1ab05c9c292","description":"Greenpeace","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e24-9f95-bebca69fe741","description":"Amnesty International","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7bca-bd75-bc6a0e6fdd2a","description":"The Nature Conservancy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72de-ac30-e58b2de6821f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is undesirable to believe a proposition when there is no ground whatever for supposing it true\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bertrand Russell received the Nobel Prize in Literature for his varied writings, which championed humanitarian ideals and freedom of thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7974-bde6-eb1d744e7ced","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ace-bb83-8dba6d4606d0","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7baf-b1b4-e36ce7809868","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-749e-ba7e-e10bb0e5e159","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7890-8846-1aae2f92cb2e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Norse god acts as the watchman of the gods, guarding the rainbow bridge Bifr\u00f6st?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Heimdall is also described as having exceptionally sharp senses; some accounts say he can hear grass growing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7b60-a9d8-d8e7cdbad05e","description":"Heimdall","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79e7-a2fb-e5148d679211","description":"Thor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-799d-9a63-e8f4636d6fe3","description":"Baldur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7296-a406-bd52b3c26b3e","description":"Tyr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7aa5-b82e-74ceec47dd6d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'God is not willing to do everything, and thus take away our free will and that share of glory which belongs to us\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Niccolo Machiavelli discusses the balance between fortune and human agency in The Prince, where this line appears.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-749c-b2c2-67468b07cba3","description":"Niccolo Machiavelli","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ede-baea-4121de8c70d6","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79aa-9c42-e67c2a0ecf2d","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7d43-a7eb-42d7fd60aa46","description":"Karl Marx","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a0c-9e71-c59ed6a2c1ae","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Wisdom is power\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Sapientia potentia est, sapientia is the subject, potentia means power, and est is the verb meaning \u201cis.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7f0a-9be2-f7976ff0cfbf","description":"Sapientia potentia est","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ede-b3d2-12f87b07ebf7","description":"Hodie mihi, cras tibi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-720f-a853-203b4dd595c8","description":"Ego te provoco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7816-8176-79cc61beb9bb","description":"Melita, domi adsum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c6c-9755-13ca01358377","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes John Dalton?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John Dalton proposed that matter is made of indivisible atoms, with each element having its own type. His ideas helped lay the groundwork for modern chemistry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7016-af87-25f079a3c0a3","description":"Chemist and physicist who ade contributions to atomic theory.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ead-981d-9e4460cbbbc7","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e71-8193-fabd215a7ecc","description":"Confirmed the theory that Earth revolves around The Sun.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-760b-978f-637658cbdc64","description":"38th President of the US.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72fc-abcf-f0aeb25e6b54","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the flag flown on a short pole at the bow of a ship?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A jack is flown at the bow, while a ship\u2019s ensign is generally flown at the stern; a burgee commonly identifies a yacht club.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7768-9c4c-e51331532f56","description":"Jack","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7d18-948a-20a535bd75f6","description":"Ensign","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7fa8-b539-10ed431bef68","description":"Pennant","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-723c-a3fc-abc48ac8b972","description":"Burgee","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7465-81e2-4318b0cf12a7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Actus me invito factus non est meus actus\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The phrase means \u201cThe act done by me against my will is not my act,\u201d expressing the legal principle that criminal responsibility generally requires voluntary conduct.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ab0-a488-4b9a95ed4f05","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e2e-ab1a-9063e8bc1020","description":"To act accidentally is not to act at all","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7370-bdd9-3853cd06e756","description":"Act as if you are always being watched","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-782b-9225-d1289b1104f9","description":"The act of an honest man cannot be questioned","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-742b-b33e-e0d7fdcafcf6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the US Military\'s highest award for valor in combat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Medal of Honor is the nation\u2019s highest military decoration, reserved for conspicuous gallantry and intrepidity at risk of life, above and beyond the call of duty.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-717f-8cde-6899732749ff","description":"Medal of Honor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c99-9988-b0b860cc8215","description":"Purple Heart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-768a-82e5-364b6792efee","description":"Bronze Star","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7fdc-a216-f83a03fd9fb0","description":"Silver Star","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7b74-b3bd-d37a0769894b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'We live in the best of all possible worlds\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leibniz argued that a perfect God would create the best possible world among all possible worlds. Voltaire later satirized that optimism in Candide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-708c-8002-9cbe5e523d49","description":"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7341-a87f-68ac20bae80f","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c5e-bd86-c201d034ac32","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7981-b927-8edc4f196362","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-78f9-9ab2-727802f74b38","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the first month of the year in the Islamic calendar?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Muharram is one of four sacred months in Islam. Its name is commonly understood to mean \u201cforbidden,\u201d reflecting a traditional prohibition on warfare during the month.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-738b-b502-23e7c1fbc9e7","description":"Muharram","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77d1-b028-8cbc84899a27","description":"Ramadan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7309-9092-6855862f9717","description":"Shawwal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c88-975e-2ea7bd9fdb6f","description":"Jumada Al-Awwal","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7787-87a3-a7aa58c2b3e6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which country had its first female prime minister, Kim Campbell, serve in 1993?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Canada\u2019s Kim Campbell served for only 132 days before the Progressive Conservatives lost the 1993 federal election.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7c35-b2ac-316af68bf43e","description":"Canada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7d6b-b369-7b3a704c470c","description":"United States","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7010-9389-61d30110f62a","description":"United Kingdom","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a13-926c-3e90b374cc00","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7e43-8192-4179930f3952","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Ta\u02bdizzi-Adeni Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Afroasiatic includes the Semitic languages as well as branches such as Berber, Cushitic, and Chadic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-783e-b964-f84414418a77","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-72b2-b8b6-907a5127040c","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7d71-bc51-abfaad882abb","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7aff-a306-9c698a9d8d78","description":"Koreanic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-74e3-aca4-fb5d1b1cf3da","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In what animal form did Zeus seduce Europa?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Zeus appeared as a bull and carried Europa to Crete, where their son Minos became a legendary king.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7094-af70-56de93d6b7cf","description":"Bull","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77ef-95bf-764b0dc7a20a","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ab0-9b18-b9668224aed4","description":"Dolphin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7887-ae88-8b381ae3afc8","description":"Eagle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-73e5-8cf0-2e