 places it in the Indo-European family.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-795e-823e-154cc972af84","description":"Indo-European","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-75e0-97c2-5d792771153c","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7a00-9d50-fc1b740a21a9","description":"Japonic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-73fc-8553-ab2402cf3cbc","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-79ad-98c8-d36707545cd0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is wrong always, everywhere and for everyone, to believe anything upon insufficient evidence\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"W. K. Clifford argued that careless beliefs can shape actions and spread harm beyond the person who holds them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7bdd-89d3-6bda89124575","description":"W. K. Clifford","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7af0-97e5-9d5d580a3ae9","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-761a-bb87-695bc22fa0ae","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-71f2-aac8-ddde3953dba2","description":"Epictetus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-793e-8155-8303cf9ea643","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the Portuguese word for \'five\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cinco is also the Spanish word for five, reflecting the languages\u2019 shared Latin roots.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7ca0-8a74-7762f13ee15e","description":"Cinco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7b64-90b9-76b90c1323c1","description":"Vijf","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-70bc-9960-896d98721bc2","description":"F\u00fcnf","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-77ca-a162-2a42e8892ce8","description":"Oito","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-556c-7675-922c-a645cd1cb2f9","locale":"en-US","ca